faqs:
  - q: Can you work in an OT environment?
    a: Yes. We respect the constraints. OT network segmentation stays intact. Data flows across a boundary designed with the plant engineering team, not around it.
  - q: Do you do SCADA or PLC programming?
    a: Not directly. We partner with specialist OT firms for the controls work and focus on the data and analytics layer above it.
  - q: What about brownfield S/4 migrations?
    a: Yes. Brownfield conversion, selective data transition, or full greenfield depending on ECC state and business drivers. We assess before recommending.
  - q: How do you handle plant-by-plant rollouts?
    a: Waves. Pilot plant first. Lessons captured. Template refined. Subsequent plants ride the template with local configuration.
  - q: Can you run the platform after go-live?
    a: Yes. See /managed-services/data-platform-operations/ and /managed-services/application-support/ for the day-two arrangement.
